      "sequence_position": 8,
      "problem": "Consider the following sequence: \n\n$$\n3,\\,6,\\,12,\\,24,\\,48,\\,…\n$$\n\nThe recursive formula for this sequence is given by\n\n${a}_{n+1}=$\n{{field-1}}$\\cdot \\,{a}_{n},$ \n$\\,{a}_{1}=$ \n{{field-2}}.",
      "worked_solution": "Notice that the first term of the sequence is ${a}_{1}=3.$\n\nInspecting the terms of the sequence, we see that we always get the next term by multiplying by $2.$\n\nTherefore, the recursive rule must be the following:\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+1}=2\\cdot {a}_{n}\\,,\\,{a}_{1}=3\n$$",
